PS5 HDMI output fixes                                     [ps5-bazzite-deck]

1. FLAVA3: after a mode above 340 MHz (4K60) turned SCDC scrambling on in the
   sink, turn it off again for lower modes; otherwise the sink shows "no
   signal" after switching from 4K down to 1080p/1080p120.
2. FLAVA3: don't program the "back to unplugged" / "back to wait resolution"
   event sequences that #43 enabled: on some TVs they make the bridge
   re-announce the sink during the first modeset, link training fails and the
   screen stays black until a re-plug.
3. Hotplug (#43): run the hotplug work on the unbound system queue (removes
   the "hogged CPU" workqueue warning).
4. Re-arm (#46): only when the same sink re-announces itself (EDID checksum);
   a different sink is set up by the hotplug path and the compositor, and
   re-arming would re-apply the previous sink's mode ("timing issue"). On
   FLAVA3 the "picture up" notification (0x04) cancels a pending re-arm, like
   Verde's 0x03 (no re-arm during the first modeset at boot).
5. Cap the output at 8 bits per colour (DRM core, PS5 only): the bridges show
   deeper colour as posterized "rainbow" contours. Drivers default "max bpc"
   to 16 and compositors may ask for 10.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index 33120dafa..20bf3621a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -1361,7 +1361,7 @@ static void dm_ps5_hotplug_handler(void *data)
 {
 	struct amdgpu_display_manager *dm = data;
 
-	queue_work(system_percpu_wq, &dm->ps5_hotplug_work);
+	queue_work(system_dfl_wq, &dm->ps5_hotplug_work);
 }
 #endif
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c
index e5c8ef06c..4ae8fe40f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic.c
@@ -568,6 +568,15 @@ static int drm_atomic_connector_check(struct drm_connector *connector,
 	struct drm_writeback_job *writeback_job = state->writeback_job;
 	const struct drm_display_info *info = &connector->display_info;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_X86_PS5
+	/*
+	 * The PS5's HDMI bridges take 8 bits per colour. Drivers default "max bpc"
+	 * to 16 and the compositor may ask for 10; deeper colour comes out as
+	 * posterized "rainbow" contours. Cap every commit at 8.
+	 */
+	if (state->max_requested_bpc > 8)
+		state->max_requested_bpc = 8;
+#endif
 	state->max_bpc = info->bpc ? info->bpc : 8;
 	if (connector->max_bpc_property)
 		state->max_bpc = min(state->max_bpc, state->max_requested_bpc);
